FORMATTER.md §6.1, §8.2 and DECISIONS 179: the comma before an item starting with "." is written
right after the item before it, ahead of that item's trailing comments.
-- in.canon --
package p

let a = { x: 1, // c
  .a: 2 }
let b = { x: 1 /* c */, .a: 2 }
-- want --
package p

let a = {
  x: 1, // c
  .a: 2
}
let b = {
  x: 1, /* c */
  .a: 2
}
